.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Verify that a macro whose identifier or parameter names are not supported by the Markdown macro syntax, or whose
.# content would not be read back as is (e.g. since one of its lines would be read as the closing tag of the macro), is
.# rendered as text, keeping its line endings, so that it's read back as the same text
.#-----------------------------------------------------
x {{info a<b>c="d"/}} {{my_macro}}<b>e</b>{{/my_macro}} f

{{my_macro}}
g

<b>h</b>
{{/my_macro}}

{{info}}
i {{info}}
{{/info}}
{{warning}}j{{/warning}}
{{/info}}
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
x \{{info a\<b>c="d"/}} \{{my\_macro}}\<b>e\</b>\{{/my\_macro}} f

\{{my\_macro}}  
g  
\
\<b>h\</b>  
\{{/my\_macro}}

\{{info}}  
i \{{info}}  
\{{/info}}  
\{{warning}}j\{{/warning}}  
\{{/info}}
